      "side": 1,
      "message": "I could not reproduce this. CMake does not shift its keyword arguments when the file list expands to nothing, so the call is a no-op rather than treating PROPERTIES as a source.\n\nMinimal case:\n\n  set(EMPTY_LIST)\n  set_source_files_properties(${EMPTY_LIST} PROPERTIES GENERATED TRUE)\n\nconfigures successfully (CMake 3.31, Ninja).\n\nOn this tree, the exact configuration described as broken also succeeds:\n\n  cmake -S . -B build -DENABLE_LIBWRAP\u003dON -DBUILD_TESTING\u003dOn\n  -- Configuring done\n  -- Generating done\n  (exit 0)\n\nThat matches the Jenkins GNU/Linux job, which builds in libwrap mode and passed.\n\nFor context, this call exists because qt_add_dbus_interface only marks the generated sources GENERATED in the top-level directory, so tests/ would otherwise look for them on disk. It is deliberately unguarded: in libwrap builds the list is empty and the call does nothing, which keeps the two modes reading the same way.",
